The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
@NonNls String tooltip = null;
tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(message.startsWith("<html>") ? XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message): XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message)) + link;
```
Reason:
The incorrect placement of parentheses in the concatenation expression causes the `link` to be appended to the `tooltip` string before it is wrapped in HTML. This results in the `link` not being included in the tooltip correctly, leading to incomplete warning displays in the editor.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml((message.startsWith("<html>") ? XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message): XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message)) + link);
```
Reason:
By moving the parentheses to encompass the entire concatenation of the message and the `link`, the `tooltip` string is now correctly constructed and wrapped in HTML. This ensures that all warnings, including the associated links, are displayed properly in the editor.

